<title>USA: Neurobiological says Dynorphin A cuts pain.</title>
<headline>Neurobiological says Dynorphin A cuts pain.</headline>
<dateline>RICHMOND, Calif. 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Neurobiological Technologies Inc said a pilot Phase II clinical trial of peptide Dynorphin A showed it reduced the amount of morphine required for management of post-surgical pain.</p>
<p>The results indicate that patients receiving Dynorphin A required substantially less morphine than those receiving placebo while experiencing comparable relief from pain during the initial 24 hours following major orthopedic surgery, it said.</p>
</text>
